    "body": "Ah, I'm not discussing putting consecutive block elements in a row but rather, that it's currently not possible to have nested block elements inside a paragraph. If block elements were to be nested within a `<p></p>`, then tag omission enforces that these become _pushed_ outside the paragraph when a browser parses HTML, before rendering a page.\r\n\r\nSee this example:\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n  <head>\r\n    <style>\r\n      div {\r\n        background-color: tomato;\r\n      }\r\n      p .complex-component {\r\n        border-style: outset;\r\n        border-radius: 3px;\r\n        background-color: dodgerblue;\r\n      }\r\n      p .complex-component:active {\r\n        border-style: inset;\r\n        background-color: blue;\r\n      }\r\n    </style>\r\n  </head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    <div class=\"page\">\r\n      <p>Click the blue button: <div class=\"complex-component\">I am blue</div></p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\nIf you run it in any browser, you will not get the desired effect of a blue colored button due to tag omission.\r\n\r\nBut if you instead run this:\r\n```html\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html>\r\n  <head>\r\n    <style>\r\n      div {\r\n        background-color: tomato;\r\n      }\r\n      p .complex-component {\r\n        border-style: outset;\r\n        border-radius: 3px;\r\n        background-color: dodgerblue;\r\n      }\r\n      p .complex-component:active {\r\n        border-style: inset;\r\n        background-color: blue;\r\n      }\r\n    </style>\r\n  </head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    <div class=\"page\">\r\n      <p>Click the blue button: <span class=\"complex-component\">I am actually blue</span></p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\nIt works as expected since spans aren't block elements, hence not triggering tag omission too early.\r\n\r\nSo the point I want to make here is that developers should be allowed to use block elements such as `<div>` inside paragraphs, for example by updating the specification so that tag omission can be turned off entirely or on a per element type basis.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
