    "updated_at": "2023-05-05T06:34:10Z",
    "body": "I realize that I have missed an important detail in my previous comments. I understand what you mean, given that. My apologies!\r\n\r\nWhat I meant was that, similar to how it is possible to put for example an `<img>`, which is structurally a block, in a paragraph, it should be possible to put a `<div>` in conjunction with `display: inline-block` in a paragraph.\r\n\r\nThis way, it would be possible to construct an inline element that has a complex internal block structure, for which, a `<div>` would be the most natural choice for organizing its internal structure.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
