    "updated_at": "2023-05-05T14:26:12Z",
    "body": "I disagree, that example is not equivalent to the example i am discussing above, which is:\r\n```html\r\n<p>Paragraph starts here <img ... > and continues here.</p>\r\n```\r\nwhich results in \r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/122010116/236478455-ef0f9a7b-0e27-4ec2-a6e2-237cb2ad033a.png)\r\nwhile with a `<div>`, it's not possible right now to achieve the same effect:\r\n```html\r\n<p>Paragraph starts here <div style=\"display: inline-block;\">An interlude.</div> and continues here.</p>\r\n```\r\nAgain, what I'm asking for is to be able to turn tag omission off so that it's possible to construct an inline element, for which, a `<div>` would be the most natural choice for organizing its internal structure, that can be used inside `<p>`-tags.",
