    "created_at": "2023-05-08T08:23:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-08T08:23:56Z",
    "body": "@scottaohara, we are in fact using `<span>` right now, since `<div>` is not an option. This is not a question of _we can't build the components we need_, but rather why we should be limited to use elements less suited as building blocks, why not give developers the option to choose? In the spirit of [WYSIWYM](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WYSIWYM), it at least seems to me that `<div>` better conveys the idea of an internal block structure than a `<span>`, even if the component as a whole is supposed to be an inline element.\r\n\r\n@annevk, fair enough, have a good one!",
